1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,934
In this town, every kid grows wings on their tenth birthday.

2
00:00:03,089 --> 00:00:04,868
The bigger your wings, the higher you rank.

3
00:00:05,086 --> 00:00:06,193
Sparrow wings are weak.

4
00:00:06,375 --> 00:00:07,539
Eagle wings are strong.

5
00:00:07,705 --> 00:00:10,623
Griffin wings, one kid in a thousand, rule the sky.

6
00:00:10,869 --> 00:00:13,223
But on my tenth birthday, I grew moth wings.

7
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,105
Grey, and the size of my hands.

8
00:00:15,335 --> 00:00:17,450
The whole square laughed before they'd even opened.

9
00:00:17,665 --> 00:00:20,075
For two years, even the little kids flicked them for fun.

10
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:22,816
But whenever someone smaller got picked on, I stepped in.

11
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,595
I knew exactly how the bottom felt.

12
00:00:24,914 --> 00:00:28,627
Then at the Sky Festival, the duke's son cornered a first-year at the edge of the cliff.

13
00:00:28,837 --> 00:00:31,337
His wings were griffin gold, wider than a wagon.

14
00:00:31,559 --> 00:00:32,420
I stepped between them.

15
00:00:32,608 --> 00:00:34,157
The whole cliff burst out laughing.

16
00:00:34,344 --> 00:00:36,148
"A moth is going to stop a griffin?"

17
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:38,035
He grinned and dove straight at me.

18
00:00:38,237 --> 00:00:40,171
An arm's length from my face, he stopped.

19
00:00:40,352 --> 00:00:41,327
Frozen in midair.

20
00:00:41,626 --> 00:00:42,757
Nobody understood why.

21
00:00:43,048 --> 00:00:47,163
Then every pair of wings on that cliff folded, and every kid dropped to one knee.

22
00:00:47,378 --> 00:00:48,477
And my wings opened.

23
00:00:48,665 --> 00:00:49,353
All the way.

24
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:50,313
They blocked out the s—

